{"title":"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>UNIVERSITY OF NORTHERN COLORADO MATHEMATICS CONTEST FINAL ROUND February 13,1993.\n</p><p>For Colorado Students Grades 7-12.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many times must one shoot at this target, and which rings must one hit in order to score exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca92e43d47d5fa16d0bd1cd84cb92dee8d52e9d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),1),black); draw(circle((0,0),2),black); draw(circle((0,0),3),black); draw(circle((0,0),4),black); draw(circle((0,0),5),black); draw(circle((0,0),6),black); MP(&quot;40&quot;,(0,0-.3),N); MP(&quot;39&quot;,(0,1-.1),N); MP(&quot;24&quot;,(0,2-.1),N); MP(&quot;23&quot;,(0,3-.1),N); MP(&quot;17&quot;,(0,4-.1),N); MP(&quot;16&quot;,(0,5-.1),N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the digit in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db43972a31bb85737768e51aa1076120bf5f178c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$623^{rd}$\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> place after the decimal point in the repeating decimal for:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387a5a2b63baa05702f1c04e43386006d0f7cd42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{99}+\\frac{3}{999}.\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A student thinks of four numbers. She adds them in pairs to get the six sums <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb90f5600a75999eff9e5c6499260f79f3112628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9,18,21,23,26,35.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />  \nWhat are the four numbers? There are two different solutions.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The table gives some of the straight line distances between certain pairs of cities. for example the distance\nbetween city <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and city <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/263fa63f962aa848483d27ca7cf8286fd5c77013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> Use the given data to determine the distance between city <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and city <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n(Hint: a problem in the first round was similar in spirit to this one.)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875589aaf1c4017093d241e0946e98083b3e7261.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{c|cccc} &amp; A &amp; B &amp; C &amp; D \\\\ \\hline A &amp; 34 &amp; &amp; 16 \\\\  B &amp; &amp; 42 &amp; \\\\  C &amp; &amp; &amp; 12\\\\  D &amp; 30 &amp; &amp; \\\\  \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"100\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive positive integers adds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b434ebc2071e706df740975a3c90aad3cfa1455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> What are the smallest and largest integers in this collection?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf8af785fd4feed6700c123d56d09de8ce6939a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2^2+3^2+6^2 &amp;= 7^2 \\\\ 3^2+4^2+12^2 &amp;= 13^2 \\\\ 4^2+5^2+20^2 &amp;= 21^2 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"151\" height=\"72\" />\n</p><p>(a) Find integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b7faa33f9c3985c1152e40a327c6d0a1210ed32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2+6^2+x^2=y^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) Conjecture a general rule that is being illustrated here.\n</p><p>(c) Prove your conjecture.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Choose four numbers by circling exactly one number in each horizontal row, and one number in each vertical column.\nCompute the product of these four numbers. Explain clearly why the same product results no matter which selection \nof this type of four numbers you make.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fed477a4de2d3ce8ef324a91f02235365d0fe6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{|cccc|} \\hline 10 &amp; 15 &amp; 35 &amp; 20 \\\\ 2&amp; 3&amp; 7&amp; 4\\\\ 8&amp; 12&amp; 28&amp; 16\\\\ 12&amp; 18&amp; 42&amp; 24\\\\ \\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"81\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For what integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the expression\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d87dd5c5681bbe1b1159dbd806c337306aa8f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}+\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{4}}+\\cdots +\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}+\\sqrt{n+1}}\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"42\" />\nequal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;? (Hint: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/315a1648e969e2c4a3f11a4d7a799ac0d3e44905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+\\sqrt{2})(1-\\sqrt{2})=-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"24\" />)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point inside the rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b317ce3508ee6fd7a08a1a9d8461c33e000d95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=5$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1452f66715e76cec0b44c93c0d71383cc1b1998b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a7049e9a8f05b14292406830d4b34ee2e66440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783d500281f8f46167dff3b071c543d42150e67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />. \n(Hint: draw helpful vertical and horizontal lines.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5c11133ade1b8f6d288e91b6d710637a5ee630.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair P=(2,2); draw((0,0)--(0,5)--(10,5)--(10,0)--cycle,dot); draw((0,0)--P,black); draw((0,5)--P,black); draw((10,5)--P,black); draw((10,0)--P,black); dot(P); MP(&quot;P&quot;,(1,1),N); MP(&quot;5&quot;,(1.5,2.9),N); MP(&quot;10&quot;,(6.5,2.8),N); MP(&quot;11&quot;,(6.5,.9),N); MP(&quot;A&quot;,(0,5),NW); MP(&quot;B&quot;,(10,5),NE); MP(&quot;C&quot;,(10,0),SE); MP(&quot;D&quot;,(0,0),SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The scalene triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e5ec10b802d2c4ee3e36981c70b593b1100405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51, 52, 53.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f6f7cd16a47f33bebcf3fc361eeb808b630504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC.$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f591d390f2c7453f1a1db5777dcbe9eed30220a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(52,0)--(24,sqrt(3)*26)--cycle); draw((24,0)--(24,sqrt(3)*26)); draw((0,-8)--(52,-8),arrow=Arrow()); draw((52,-8)--(0,-8),arrow=Arrow()); draw((24,3)--(21,3)--(21,0),black); MP(&quot;B&quot;,(0,0),SW);MP(&quot;A&quot;,(24,sqrt(3)*26),N);MP(&quot;C&quot;,(52,0),SE);MP(&quot;D&quot;,(24,0),S); MP(&quot;52&quot;,(26,-8),S);MP(&quot;53&quot;,(38,sqrt(3)*13),NE);MP(&quot;51&quot;,(12,sqrt(3)*13),NW); [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>(a) Determine the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0edb6ba307f77287794310f53f3d7586c5ff6d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD.$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>(b) Determine the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd222166def59a3315433877917a826de6488031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017093931\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 205/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7777/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13615:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017093931 and revision id 65345. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}